WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:08.160
Few years ago, a wave of Vitamin A deficiency

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.651
hit many parts of the globe.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.880
The deficiency was so severe that it resulted

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.860
in several deaths within no time!

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.240
What could have been done to crack this problem?

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.500
Scientists soon realised that the staple food

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:25.939
of most of the areas hit by this disaster

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:28.180
was Rice.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.020
They took efforts to modify rice in such a

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.840
way that it produced the necessary compound

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.850
in the body when consumed.

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.240
With this, the concept of Golden rice emerged!

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.480
It’s a variety of rice that is capable of

00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.640
biosynthesizing beta-carotene which is a precursor

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:51.860
of vitamin A. When consumed, the beta-carotene

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:55.430
is readily converted to Vitamin A in the body,

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.120
thus saving uncountable lives!

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.800
Doesn’t this sound like science fiction?

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.540
It definitely does, but this has actually happened!

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:08.240
Let me make it more interesting!

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.820
Imagine there is one single plant that has

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:14.890
potatoes in the root and tomatoes at the shoot!

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:16.620
Do you think this is possible?

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.280
Of course it is!

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.600
This variety is called Pomato: a plant that

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.480
bears 2 edible parts in the same body!

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.480
And now for the last one!

00:01:28.490 --> 00:01:31.237
Imagine you’re in a dark room and suddenly

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:34.020
you find a fluorescently glowing mice running

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:35.020
around!

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:38.610
Do you think this kind of glowing mice exist?

00:01:39.440 --> 00:01:40.980
Yes they do!

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.920
The concept of fluorescent mice is no longer

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.380
fiction because there are transgenic mice

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.580
which glow with fluorescence!

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:52.200
Why are we looking at these examples?

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.760
We know that Computers run on codes, and so

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:57.900
do our bodies!

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:00.040
Just like there are specific codes for running

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.840
a computer, we have specific codes for organisms’

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.260
body design.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:08.760
And any change in these codes, can give us

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:12.070
miraculous results like the golden rice, the

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.740
Pomato plant and the glowing mice!

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:18.160
And the study of all these wonderful concepts

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:20.710
is nothing but “GENETICS”!

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:24.280
We have come across this term several times!

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.760
Genetics finds applications not only in modern

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.520
day research but even answers various queries

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.740
that pop up in our minds.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.440
Many of us assume that genetics is only about the

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:40.580
characters passed on to children from their

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:44.040
parents, but is it as simple as that?

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:48.300
And even if we know or assume things, it is

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.520
important to ask the question ‘Why’.

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.605
For instance, have you ever wondered why an

00:02:54.605 --> 00:02:57.690
apple tree only gives rise to another apple tree?

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.480
Why don’t we get a banana or a mango tree from it?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.900
Why does a cat gives birth to only a kitten?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.240
And why do humans give birth to humans only?

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.820
Well you may say, that the answer is nature!

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:12.820
Okay!

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.080
So now can you tell me that if a human gives

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:17.420
birth to another human, then why are those

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:19.360
two not exactly the same?

00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:23.440
Why do we find each individual unique?

00:03:23.960 --> 00:03:27.060
What makes the kid strikingly different from

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.710
his or her parents?

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:31.440
Well, there are endless questions that pop

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:33.650
up in our minds.

00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.720
And how do we find answers to them?

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.060
That's where the branch of “Genetics ” comes into play.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.260
In this lesson, and in the upcoming one's, let's

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:46.280
get introduced to this branch and try answering

00:03:46.280 --> 00:03:49.120
all the questions that pop-up in our minds

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.480
about the living world around us!

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:54.200
To begin with, let's define Genetics.

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:57.200
In simple terms, it can be defined as the

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.620
branch of Biology that deals with heredity

00:04:00.620 --> 00:04:02.260
and genetic variation .

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.820
Now you may wonder what do these two terms mean?

00:04:06.260 --> 00:04:09.560
To begin our studies on genetics, we

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:12.080
need to first understand a few terms in detail.

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:15.740
Let us begin with understanding what heredity is!

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.500
Let’s assume this is one happy family . Now

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.460
if we observe this kid, he has a few features

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:25.520
like his dad and a few like his mom!

00:04:26.169 --> 00:04:28.340
That is because he has got these features

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:30.020
from each parent.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.720
This passing of traits or characters from

00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:36.480
one generation to the other is nothing but heredity!

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:40.660
So we can define heredity as passing of traits

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:43.100
from parents to their offsprings.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.080
Now what do we exactly mean by Traits and characters?

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:47.800
It’s simple!

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.740
In this case , the child has black coloured

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:52.580
eyes just like his mom.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.600
The father however has blue coloured eyes.

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:59.120
Now here we have two different types of eye

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:01.360
colours, black and blue.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.380
Similarly, there are many other colours of

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:05.940
eyes that exist in nature.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:09.320
So the eye colour is the character.

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:12.920
The eye colour can vary among the population of a

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.680
particular species.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.300
On the other hand, trait will be black or

00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.940
blue colour of the eyes, which is exclusive

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:22.060
for that particular individual.

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.436
To take another example, height is a character,

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.930
while tall and short are the traits.

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:32.140
Hair colour is a character, while black and

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:33.800
blonde are the traits.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:36.480
So the passing of these traits from one generation

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:40.200
to the other is called heredity . And what

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:42.780
has got passed to the next generation is usually

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.980
referred to as Inheritance!

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.120
Now tell me one thing.

00:05:48.140 --> 00:05:50.760
If this boy has inherited the traits from

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.860
his parents, why is he not the exact copy

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:55.509
of either of the parent?

00:05:55.509 --> 00:05:59.550
I mean why does he look slightly different from both?

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:03.400
The answer lies in the single term called “variation”.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:06.800
Isn’t the term self-explanatory?

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:10.880
As the name says, it means differences.

00:06:10.880 --> 00:06:13.620
So variations are the differences that make

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:16.380
one organism different from its parents.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.809
As in this case, the boy has inherited a few

00:06:19.809 --> 00:06:22.640
traits from his mom and a few from his dad.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.020
But he is different from both!

00:06:25.350 --> 00:06:29.240
Thus, there are many variations in him!

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.759
These basics in genetics are known to us now.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:35.440
But ever wondered who laid the foundations

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:37.280
of this interesting subject?

00:06:37.780 --> 00:06:39.820
Who were the pioneers in genetics that helped

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:42.000
us crack the code of life?

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.740
Let's have a glance at the history of genetics

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:47.300
in the upcoming part!

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.759
This image of evolution is not new to us!

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:56.840
But ever wondered how species evolved?

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:00.460
How are a few factors eliminated and a few

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:01.840
carried forward?

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.380
Well, the answers are obtained when we combine

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:08.180
evolutionary studies with genetics!

00:07:08.180 --> 00:07:11.100
Many scientists have been working on genetics

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.180
since ages.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:15.160
But there was one legendary figure who could

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:18.420
answer why a green pea plant gave rise to

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:20.480
another similar green pea plant.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.180
Let's get back in time to understand how

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:27.040
the foundations of Genetics were laid!

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:30.540
Genetic studies were carried out since the

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:33.580
classical era wherein scientists like Aristotle

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:36.840
and Hippocrates had put forth a few theories

00:07:36.840 --> 00:07:39.730
regarding how parental characters are passed

00:07:39.730 --> 00:07:41.380
to the next generation.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:44.540
However, a breakthrough was achieved when

00:07:44.543 --> 00:07:47.860
an Augustinian friar carried out remarkable

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:51.380
experiments using garden pea plants and laid

00:07:51.380 --> 00:07:54.000
the foundations of modern day genetics.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.220
It was around the nineteenth century that

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:59.960
Gregor Johan Mendel , now known as the “father

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:02.420
of genetics” performed the experiments that

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.280
lead him to this path.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.320
Mendel, while working in a garden wondered

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.000
why the green pea plants with one particular

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.340
trait gave rise to plants with the same trait…

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:17.240
For example , plants with purple flowers gave

00:08:17.240 --> 00:08:20.199
rise to plants with purple flowers only.

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:22.480
So,Why is this so?

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:25.400
And Why do white colour flowered plants give plants

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:27.480
with white colour flowers only?

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:32.280
And what will happen if these two varieties are crossed?

00:08:32.289 --> 00:08:35.387
With all these queries in mind, Mendel decided

00:08:35.387 --> 00:08:38.149
to carry out a few experiments that would

00:08:38.149 --> 00:08:41.519
help him find out the answers.

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.480
But where did he think all these experiments

00:08:43.480 --> 00:08:44.440
would take him?

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:47.740
How did he think of beginning with the procedures?

00:08:48.160 --> 00:08:51.260
And what were the list of requirements he gathered?

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:53.840
What could have been the possible conclusions?

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.240
Let us try answering all these questions one by one!

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.900
To begin with, let's understand WHY did Gregor

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.520
Mendel chose Pisum sativum, commonly known

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.100
as the green pea plant.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:10.920
Mendel knew that for his experiments, he would

00:09:10.920 --> 00:09:13.379
require a plant which is perennial and not

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.440
annual.

00:09:15.140 --> 00:09:18.240
In literal terms, perennial means something

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.840
that can last for a long time.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:23.500
Here it meant the plant than can grow and

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:25.820
reproduce in a recurring fashion.

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:29.260
Secondly, the plant should have a small life cycle.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.240
It should be able to grow quickly.

00:09:32.250 --> 00:09:35.180
Also, Mendel wanted a plant that would not

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:38.380
require too many exclusive conditions to grow.

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.360
Minimal requirements should suffice

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:42.720
the growth of the plant.

00:09:42.960 --> 00:09:45.740
Most importantly, to understand the results

00:09:45.747 --> 00:09:48.559
of crossing different varieties better, Mendel

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:51.400
required contrasting traits in the plants.

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.880
That means one character should have two contrasting

00:09:54.880 --> 00:09:56.499
traits.

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:58.780
For example, the flower colour in green peas

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:02.060
is purple and in some it's white.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.940
Purple and white are the contrasting traits

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:06.200
that can help in the study!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.420
So which were the contrasting characters that

00:10:10.420 --> 00:10:12.640
Mendel found in the green pea plants?

00:10:13.340 --> 00:10:15.680
There were seven pairs of contrasting characters

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:18.980
in total chosen by Mendel in the plant.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:21.200
Here they are

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:24.019
The first character Mendel chose was height

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:27.220
of the plant . The contrasting traits were

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:29.020
tall and dwarf plants.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:32.440
Second character in the list was the colour

00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:35.020
of the flower . The contrasting traits were

00:10:35.029 --> 00:10:38.279
purple coloured flowers and white coloured flowers.

00:10:39.020 --> 00:10:42.081
And the third character on the list was position

00:10:42.081 --> 00:10:44.760
of the flower . That could be either axial

00:10:44.769 --> 00:10:46.579
or terminal.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.660
In simple words, Axial means the flowers shoot

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:52.700
off from the middle of the stem, and terminal

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:55.580
means that the flower is situated at the top

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:57.300
of the plant stem.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:00.580
The next character chosen was shape of the seed.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:04.220
We know that green peas have two types of

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:05.180
seeds.

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.120
One type is round and smooth, while the other

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.680
type is rough or wrinkled with scales.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:14.380
This was the next pair of contrasting traits.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:17.200
After seed shape, we have the character of

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:21.060
seed colour . The contrasting traits in this

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.280
are the green and yellow colours of the seeds.

00:11:24.800 --> 00:11:27.540
Similar to the seed colour, the next character

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:30.860
was pod colour . A pod is nothing but a case

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.460
that holds the plant’s seeds.

00:11:34.600 --> 00:11:37.040
Here the two contrasting traits were green

00:11:37.040 --> 00:11:39.820
coloured and yellow coloured pods.

00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:43.500
And the last pair of contrasting character was

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:46.680
that of pod shape . Green pea pods can either

00:11:46.680 --> 00:11:48.800
be inflated or constricted.

00:11:50.220 --> 00:11:53.120
Both these traits are contrasting!

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:56.620
With these seven pairs of contrasting characters,

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:59.040
Mendel began his experiments.

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:01.920
Little did he know that he was building the

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.980
foundation of modern genetics…

00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.900
Let's have a look at what his experiments

00:12:06.906 --> 00:12:10.040
were and the conclusions he derived from them

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:11.460
in the next part.

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.980
We have taken a look at the seven pairs of

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:19.879
contrasting characters chosen by Gregor Mendel

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.600
for his experiments on the green pea plant.

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:26.060
so here is a table that gives us an idea of what

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.260
the contrasting characters and their respective

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.060
traits were !

00:12:30.880 --> 00:12:33.340
Now can you guess how Mendel thought of this

00:12:33.340 --> 00:12:34.340
experiment?

00:12:35.100 --> 00:12:37.620
How was it exactly planned by Mendel?

00:12:37.980 --> 00:12:39.540
What was his aim?

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:42.360
Well, Mendel thought of beginning with trying

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.600
to understand what happens on crossing the

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.900
plants with contrasting traits.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:50.200
Mendel, just like others, knew that a plant

00:12:50.201 --> 00:12:52.879
with purple flowers gives us another plant

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.149
with purple flowers only.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.720
And it's the same case with a plant that has white

00:12:57.720 --> 00:12:59.440
coloured flowers.

00:12:59.680 --> 00:13:02.220
Now Mendel was curious to know, what will

00:13:02.226 --> 00:13:04.949
happen if a purple flowered plant is crossed

00:13:04.949 --> 00:13:06.940
with the white flowered variety?

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:10.720
Ideally the result has to be flowers with

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.180
intermediate colours.

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.040
But was that actually what Mendel got?

00:13:15.920 --> 00:13:18.260
Let's have a look at the results in detail.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.060
But before that , do you know how crossing

00:13:21.060 --> 00:13:22.880
is carried out?

00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:27.100
Well, the male and female plants are selected first.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:30.780
Now the pea plant being bisexual, has both

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:32.980
male and female reproductive parts in the

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:34.649
same plant.

00:13:34.649 --> 00:13:37.620
So we can choose the purple flower to be male

00:13:37.620 --> 00:13:40.300
and the white flower to be female or vice

00:13:40.300 --> 00:13:41.540
versa.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.160
Now the female flower on the respective plant

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:45.780
is emasculated first.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:48.760
So do you know what emasculation is?

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:53.220
As the name suggests, masculine refers to male.

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:55.740
So here, emasculation refers to the removal

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:58.259
of male reproductive parts.

00:13:59.100 --> 00:14:01.200
Let's take these two flowers to understand

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:03.320
the crossing process in detail.

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:07.780
Now the anther of this flower will be removed.

00:14:08.460 --> 00:14:11.800
Removal of anthers makes sure that the flower

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:13.600
will not get self-pollinated.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:17.040
Now this exclusive female flower is dusted

00:14:17.048 --> 00:14:19.949
with the pollen grains from this male flower,

00:14:19.949 --> 00:14:21.880
which ensures pollination.

00:14:22.580 --> 00:14:25.980
And the successful fertilisation will be ensured

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:27.920
when the plant develops flowers!

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:30.620
This is how crossing is carried out!

00:14:31.100 --> 00:14:33.740
Now let us get back to Mendel’s experiments.

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.680
Mendel crossed a plant with purple flowers

00:14:36.680 --> 00:14:38.940
and a plant with white flowers.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:42.800
He expected results in which the plants obtained

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.740
will be intermediate between purple and white.

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:49.910
But to his astonishment, he obtained all the

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:52.620
plants in the progeny to be purple coloured!

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.700
Unexpected right?

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:56.720
And this doesn’t stop here!

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:00.140
On crossing the purple coloured flowers from

00:15:00.140 --> 00:15:02.879
this progeny with each other, he got another

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.680
set of astonishing results!

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.720
If purple flowered plants are crossed among

00:15:07.720 --> 00:15:10.900
each other, we should obtain which variety?

00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:14.020
We would get all plants with purple coloured

00:15:14.020 --> 00:15:16.640
flowers, is what most of us would think!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:19.960
But to his astonishment, Mendel obtained a

00:15:19.960 --> 00:15:22.559
few plants with white coloured flowers as

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:23.180
well!

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:27.540
So on an average, he obtained 75% plants with

00:15:27.540 --> 00:15:31.980
purple flowers and 25% plants with white flowers.

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.880
How could this be possible now?

00:15:35.440 --> 00:15:38.080
Let us try and understand these results in

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:39.680
the next part!

